{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/34839-the-star-wars-conversion-to-the-cwod-nwod-systems","id":34839,"title":"the Star Wars conversion to the CWOD/NWOD systems","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-22T00:50:29-08:00","id":34839,"title":"the Star Wars conversion to the CWOD/NWOD systems","content":"I remember hearing a bit about some fan projects in the work a year or two ago, is anybody still working on this? I've done my own conversions using the Mage the Dark Ages magic system as a basis for the force powers (with some tweaks) and ran more than a few good games but I'd like to hear what other's have done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T01:26:30-08:00","id":34851,"title":"","content":"I ran a Star Wars campaign back in the 90's using the Vampire ruleset (Celerity, Potence, Thaumaturgy, etc). I don't have those notes anymore more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T23:00:41-08:00","id":35395,"title":"","content":"WOW, vamp disciplines as force powers eh?<br /> <br /> I made up a slew of force powers and used the dark ages mage system as my basis for the force powers, we used to jokingly call the game Jedi: The Force because of the WOD style focus on playing supernaturals, my players were encouraged to play force users and the games had a very mystical focus.<br /> <br /> We used Dark Ages Mage's magic system because it was so versatile, we changed the foundation attribute to 'force connection/sensitivity' which reflected the force users basic connection to the force and made over 30 pillars which were all based on the force powers. I'm slowly typing out and revising my notes on all the force powers and the tweaks if any ones interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","user":"Dream_Walker","date":". 12-23-2013, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1123-dream_walker","name":"Dream_Walker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}